--TEST--
A PHP `function (…) use (…) { … }` literal and an `fn` parameter with no type and no parameter to take one from are refused, each with its own code — `rule:types/callable-values`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: tools:php-differences/closures-and-callables
int $k = 3;
function (int $x) use ($k) { return $x + $k; };
fn($x) => $x;
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0222]: anonymous `function` literals are not supported
%A
error[E0223]: closures have no `use` clause
%A
error[E0808]: this parameter has no type, and no position to take one from
%A
error: aborting due to 3 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
